      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1714701195356,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "if there was a valid edge (minWeight != INFINITY), then\nexecute the necessary assignments:\n    1) increment your new graph's edgeCount\n    2) add your new graph's minCost to to the minWeight\n    3) assign the pair of edges (u, v) with the least minWeight to your new graph\n    4) assign the respective pair of edges' weight\n    5) VERY IMPORTANT, in your BV Set of visited vertices, update your vertex\n    at visited[v] where v represents the TAIL of your respective pair of edges. We\n    choose to update using the tail (v) since it's the vertex we are connecting to.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "if there was a valid edge (minWeight != INFINITY), then\nexecute the necessary assignments:\n    1) increment your new graph's edgeCount\n    2) add your new graph's minCost to to the minWeight\n    3) assign the pair of edges (u, v) with the least minWeight to your new graph\n    4) assign the respective pair of edges' weight\n    5) VERY IMPORTANT, in your BV Set of visited vertices, update your vertex\n    at visited[v] where v represents the TAIL of your respective pair of edges. We\n    choose to update using the tail (v) since it's the vertex we are connecting to.",
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
